  "log": [
    "====================================================================================================",
    "NEXUS SPHERE COVERAGE ON REAL DNA -- how far does a single-atom change actually reach?",
    "====================================================================================================",
    "  The proposal: tile chromatin's DNA in ~4 A overlapping spheres, run NEXUS chemistry in each,",
    "  and let overlap carry a single-atom change across the structure. A sphere of radius R around",
    "  an atom IS an interaction truncation at R, so 'is 4 A enough' has an exact answer on a real",
    "  structure. Reference = every pair, no cutoff. Nothing here is compared against a model.",
    "  NEXUS's OWN cutoffs: LJ 6 A, desolvation 8 A, electrostatics 10 A, induction 10 A -- every one",
    "  larger than the proposed 4 A sphere. That is a reason to measure, not a proof.",
    "\n  1KX5: 16755 atoms | 6021 DNA | 3130 ordered water | 7604 histone+ion",
    "  147 bp on a histone octamer at 1.9 A -- chromatin at atomic resolution, small enough to be exact.",
    "  PERTURBATION: atom 3030 (OP1 of DT chain J) charge -0.78 -> +0.22. One atom.",
    "\n  Precomputing the static field at all 16k atoms in a single O(N^2) pass per arm...",
    "    dna_charged  (the case) done at 67s",
    "    dna_screened (control) done at 100s",
    "    dna_neutral  (control) done at 128s",
    "    shuffled_chg (control) done at 156s",
    "\n  ARM 1 -- REACH: fraction of the TOTAL |response| captured inside radius R.",
    "  Absolute, not signed: a signed fraction can read 100% while a large positive and a large",
    "  negative in the far field merely cancel, and cancellation is not capture.",
    "    arm                            4A      6A      8A     10A     12A     16A     20A     24A     32A     40A",
    "    dna_charged  (the case)     0.350   0.396   0.443   0.478   0.499   0.548   0.592   0.625   0.705   0.763",
    "    dna_screened (control)      0.721   0.809   0.886   0.919   0.937   0.961   0.977   0.986   0.995   0.998",
    "    dna_neutral  (control)      0.431   0.467   0.508   0.540   0.558   0.600   0.639   0.667   0.737   0.788",
    "    shuffled_chg (control)      0.456   0.516   0.542   0.564   0.577   0.620   0.653   0.678   0.740   0.789",
    "\n  ARM 2 -- THE SHELL-INTEGRATED RESPONSE, which is the decisive curve and is NOT the per-atom",
    "  decay. For a kernel U ~ q q / r^2 the atom count in a shell grows as r^2 while the interaction",
    "  falls as r^-2, so the shell SUM can stay flat while the per-atom response decays reassuringly.",
    "  A per-atom plot would look convergent for a sum that is not.",
    "    dna_charged  (the case)   (kcal/mol per shell, |.| = absolute)",
    "            0-4      4-8     8-12    12-16    16-20    20-25    25-30    30-40    40-50    50-70",
    "         812.69   216.05   131.12   111.81   103.10   101.71   122.65   172.20   126.87   169.19",
    "    dna_screened (control)   (kcal/mol per shell, |.| = absolute)",
    "            0-4      4-8     8-12    12-16    16-20    20-25    25-30    30-40    40-50    50-70",
    "         209.44    47.96    14.87     6.94     4.64     2.82     1.97     1.37     0.35     0.10",
    "    dna_neutral  (control)   (kcal/mol per shell, |.| = absolute)",
    "            0-4      4-8     8-12    12-16    16-20    20-25    25-30    30-40    40-50    50-70",
    "        1083.31   192.49   127.53   105.61    96.51    94.00   116.53   165.52   120.11   161.69",
    "    shuffled_chg (control)   (kcal/mol per shell, |.| = absolute)",
    "            0-4      4-8     8-12    12-16    16-20    20-25    25-30    30-40    40-50    50-70",
    "        1332.77   254.20   102.10   124.78    97.69   100.57   118.10   177.78   153.43   189.07",
    "\n  ARM 3 -- FIDELITY per distance shell: truncated (= sphere of radius R) vs exact.",
    "  rel.err = sum|trunc-exact| / sum|exact|.  slope = regression of truncated on exact; a scheme",
    "  that is right up to a uniform factor scores pearson 1.0 and slope != 1, so slope is the",
    "  number that matters. Metrics over LIVE atoms only -- matched zeros would manufacture r ~ 1.",
    "    sphere R = 4 A     total |response| exact 2322.7 vs truncated 335.4 kcal/mol (14.4% of it)",
    "      shell          atoms   live   rel.err   slope  pearson",
    "      0-4 A              8      8     1.079  -0.154   -0.532",
    "      4-8 A             34     34     1.000   0.000      nan",
    "      8-12 A            41     41     1.000   0.000      nan",
