    "    sphere R = 20 A     total |response| exact 2322.7 vs truncated 609.8 kcal/mol (26.3% of it)",
    "      shell          atoms   live   rel.err   slope  pearson",
    "      0-4 A              8      8     0.767   0.216    0.552",
    "      4-8 A             34     34     0.545   0.554    0.829",
    "      8-12 A            41     41     0.559   0.472    0.830",
    "      12-20 A          202    201     0.667   0.404    0.765",
    "      20-35 A         1039    972     1.000   0.000      nan",
    "      35-60 A         4214   2423     1.000   0.000      nan",
    "\n  READING",
    "  TRUNCATION DOES NOT MERELY LOSE THE FAR FIELD, IT CORRUPTS THE NEAR ONE. In the 0-4 A shell",
    "  -- entirely INSIDE the 4 A sphere, where the scheme should be exact -- the slope against",
    "  the true response is -0.154 and the correlation -0.532.",
    "  The reason is induction: its energy is -1/2 (alpha/KE)|E|^2, a SQUARE of a sum, so the",
    "  change contains a cross term 2*E0.dE that multiplies the perturbation by the PRE-EXISTING",
    "  field. Truncating corrupts E0, and a wrong E0 inside the sphere is enough to flip the sign",
    "  of the answer there. No sphere size fixes a term that is a square of a truncated sum.",
    "  A 4 A sphere captures 35.0% of the unscreened response and 72.1% of the screened one.",
    "  UNSCREENED: no radius in the sweep reaches 90%. The sphere scheme cannot represent bare",
    "  Coulomb on DNA at ANY size short of the whole particle -- the fix is not a bigger sphere,",
    "  it is a far-field channel (Ewald/multipole), which is a different proposal.",
    "  SCREENED (150 mM, Debye 7.9 A): 90% captured at R = 10 A. Screening is what makes",
    "  a local scheme legitimate -- but NEXUS does not screen, so this is a change to the physics",
    "  rather than a vindication of the tiling as it stands.",
    "\n  total 156s  -> outputs/orphan/nexus_dna_spheres.json"
  ]
}